    "id": "c003",
    "name": "1. Appointment",
    "text": "‘1, Appointment Participant has appointed Bank under other agreements as custodian of certain assets (herein “Account\"). Such agreements authorize Participant to appoint an agert to lend securities from the Account. Participant hereby appoints Wells Fargo Bank Minnesota, N.A. as Agent for the purpose of lending securities from its Account under the Wells Fargo Securities Lending Program."
  },
  {
    "id": "c004",
    "name": "Section 2(f) — Permitted Cash Investments",
    "text": "Such cash shall be invested in repurchase agreements, master notes (VPN), U.S. treasuries and agencies, U.S or Buro dollar certificates of deposit and time deposits, bankers acceptances, commercial paper, and other short term money market instruments, and mutual funds holding any of the previously mentioned securities and subject to policy and standard guidelines established from time to time by the Bank."
  },
  {
    "id": "c005",
    "name": "Section 2(f) — Safety and Liquidity Standard",
    "text": "The prime considerations for the investment portfolio shall be safety of principal and __ liquidity requirements,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c006",
    "name": "3. Allocation of Security Loans among Participants",
    "text": "3. Allocation of Security Loans among Partt ants. The Participant's securities available for lending are listed in the Securities Lending Omnibus Account as part of the lending inventory. The Bank will use reasonable efforts to allocate loans on a security by security queue basis. As a result of the queue, Participant understands that a single Borrower may bé lent a significant portion, or all, of Participant's securities available for lending."
  },
  {
    "id": "c007",
    "name": "Section 4 — Return of Collateral",
    "text": "The Bank will retum to the Borrower directly or through the Clearing Organization the collateral securing the loan."
  },
  {
    "id": "c008",
    "name": "5. Portfolio Investment Activity and Corporate Action",
    "text": "5. Portfolio Investment Activity and C rate A in Regard to Loaned Securities A Participant Account is entitled to all cash dividends, stock dividends, stock splits, rights of distribution, conversion privileges, tender and exchange offers, and similar corporate actlons with respect to any Joaned securities as if the securities had not been loaned, During apy: period when securities are loaned, the Participant waives its right to vote such secuzities. Participant may regain right to vote securities by causing a timely termination of a Joan in advance of the record date established for determining stockholder entitlement to vote. Any securities of the portfolio that are on loan may be sold by the Participant's investment manager or fiduciary at any time, The Bank must receive notice on. trade date from the proper party advising the Bank of any sale. Upon such notice, the Bank will initiate action to terminate the Joan of the secinities sold. If such notice is not received by the Bank, the Bank assumes no lability for the failure of the transaction to settle on contractual settlement date."
  },
  {
    "id": "c009",
    "name": "6. Recordkeeping and Reporting",
    "text": "6. Recordkeeping and Reporting | | The Bank will keep security loan records separate from a Participant's custodial or fiduciary portfolio records. Income from each loan will be credited to a. Participant's Account once a month, The Participant shall receive a detailed report monthly which shall include all loan activity, Borrowers to whom loans ‘were made and income eamed,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c010",
    "name": "Earnings Allocation and Fees",
    "text": "Income from the Securities Lending Program is generated by fees paid by the Borrowers and income from investment of cash collateral, All cash collateral is pooled for investment purposes, In acting as Agent for the Participant, the Bank will receive 40% on the net earnings from each loan and the Participant will receive 60%, The fees will be calculated monthly and the Bank's fee will be ' withheld from the remittance to the Participant or the Account."
  },
  {
    "id": "c011",
    "name": "Section 8 — Participant’s Investment-Loss Risk",
    "text": "8. Risk of Loss gtr : * CIC 00003 of 6 Oe A LN LTT 5 CONFIDENTIAL Participant assumes ail risk of loss arising out of Borrower defaults on retum of lent securities, collateral deficiencies or collateral investment loss,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c012",
    "name": "Section 8 — Bank’s Negligent-Operation Risk",
    "text": "The Bank dssumes the risk of loss arising from negligent and freudvlent operation of its Securities Lending Program."
