{"judgments": [
  {"clause_id": "c011",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Participant assumes all risk of loss arising out of ... collateral investment loss\" states an unqualified assumption of risk with no carve-out on its face, yet \"all risk of loss\" must somehow accommodate the Bank's own conduct. Whether it covers losses caused by the Bank's investment decisions is precisely the open term.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.42},
     {"issue": "It cannot be squared with the closing sentence of the same Section 8, under which \"The Bank assumes the risk of loss arising from negligent and fraudulent operation of its Securities Lending Program\", nor with Section 2(f)'s safety-of-principal mandate. One sentence gives the Participant all investment loss, the other gives the Bank losses from its own negligent operation.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.61}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c012",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Negligent and fraudulent operation\" is conjunctive as written, so it can be read to require both negligence and fraud before the Bank bears any loss, and \"operation of its Securities Lending Program\" does not say whether investment of cash collateral is \"operation\". The mis-typed conjunction changes the scope of the Bank's assumed risk.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.58},
     {"issue": "It directly contradicts the opening sentence of Section 8, which gives the Participant \"all risk of loss arising out of ... collateral investment loss\", leaving no rule for a collateral investment loss caused by negligent Bank operation. The two sentences of the same section allocate the identical loss to opposite parties.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.57}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c013",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The waiver sentence is internally inconsistent: it conditions waiver on \"mutual agreement\" yet says \"either party may waive all or part of the Notice period\", so it is unclear whether waiver is unilateral or bilateral. Termination is also made subject to the Borrower Security Loan Agreements, which are not part of this instrument.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.33},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.11}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c014",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The notice address names \"Copic Companies\" while the contracting party is \"Copic Insurance Company\", a discrepancy in the identity of the notice recipient. The clause also prescribes mailing only, with no timing or deemed-receipt rule.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.16},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.09}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c015",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.07},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.07}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c016",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.06},
     {"issue": "Excluding headings from construction cuts against reliance on the heading \"Risk of Loss\" and similar labels used to organise Sections 2, 4 and 8, which parties would otherwise invoke to harmonise the conflicting risk sentences. The practical effect of the exclusion on those sections could be argued.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.14}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c017",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.09},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.09}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c018",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The clause says the Agreement is \"binding on the successors and assigns\" without saying whether assignment is permitted or requires consent, so it can be read either as authorising assignment or merely as binding permitted assigns. The unaddressed assignment right is the ambiguity.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.09}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c019",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The effective date is left blank (\"on the ___ day of January, 2001\"), so the instrument does not state when it takes effect. That omission is a mechanical defect that changes when obligations began.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30},
     {"issue": "It cannot be squared with the preamble, which dates the agreement the 31st day of January 2001, or with the execution date \"7/6/2000\" in the signature block. A court would have to choose among three inconsistent dates.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.28}
   ]}
]}

